    "basis": "The exact candidate source representation has a strong direct primary-source crosswalk to the official USCB 2019 Lunda Norte polygon. A retained USCB October 2024 DRC comparison places five of the 47 Kahemba centers strictly inside its DRC ADM0/current KAHEMBA ADM2 and 42 outside; all five inside keys still retain the original Lunda Norte contact and original COD target. The bounded full-ring test against the complete 2019 USCB Lunda Norte polygon finds all five centers outside and not on its boundary, while those same centers remain hits in the pinned 2021 simplified geoBoundaries feature. This three-way pattern is consistent with simplification/generalization sensitivity, but does not establish that the 2021 hit is an erroneous artifact: the original contract evaluates the registered 2021 candidate representation and supplies no rule replacing it with the older full ring or discarding a contact after simplification changes center membership. Conversely, the 2021 hit alone does not establish territorial applicability; the 2024 DRC product is not retroactive evidence about 2021, and the vertex-subsequence crosswalk proves correspondence rather than identical geometry or transfer of attribution. The full original stock diagnostic held these cells. The independent reviewer found that the five-key result sharpens but does not resolve the source-relative conflict; no distinct reasonable public digital primary-source step likely to decide it was identified. All 47 remain held and pending, with no repair, owner change, hold removal, accepted credit, or package completion."
  },
